==DISCUSSION==

WIND GUSTS UP TO 100 KM/H ARE EXPECTED THIS AFTERNOON. 

A LINE OF SHOWERS AND WEAK THUNDERSTORMS HAS DEVELOPED WEST OF 
EDMONTON AND IS TRACKING EAST ALONG THE YELLOWHEAD CORRIDOR. STRONG 
WIND GUSTS CAN BE EXPECTED AS THIS LINE OF SHOWERS PASSES THROUGH 
THE AREA. 

WINDS WILL DIMINISH LATER THIS AFTERNOON.

DRIVING CONDITIONS WILL LIKELY BE DIFFICULT. HIGH-SIDED VEHICLES 
WILL BE PUSHED AROUND BY THE WIND. DAMAGE TO ROOFS, FENCES, BRANCHES 
OR SOFT SHELTERS IS POSSIBLE. SECURE LOOSE OBJECTS. BE PREPARED TO 
ADAPT YOUR DRIVING FOR CHANGING CONDITIONS. 

